eMetadata with 'fps' and 'totalFrames' properties, while src/providers/types.ts does not include these. This will cause type confusion and potential incompatibilities.","suggestion":"Consolidate the type definitions. Either: 1) Remove duplicates from src/types.ts and re-export from src/providers/types.ts, or 2) Ensure both definitions are identical and one imports from the other. The provider FrameMetadata (without fps) appears correct per design.md spec."},{"severity":"blocking","file":"src/providers/video-file.ts","line":0,"issue":"Test coverage for video-file.ts is only 39.21%, well below the 80% requirement. The uncovered code includes lines 215-297 (probeVideo) and 303-382 (extractFrames) - the core ffmpeg integration logic.","suggestion":"Either add more unit tests mocking the ffmpeg subprocess behavior, or consider adding integration tests that test the real ffmpeg path with actual video files to increase coverage."},{"severity":"important","file":"src/providers/media-stream.ts","line":165,"issue":"Lines 165-166 and 195-196 are not covered by tests. These appear to be null-check guards for getContext and video track checks.","suggestion":"Add test cases for when canvas.getContext('2d') returns null and when getVideoTracks() returns an empty array during getNextFrame()."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/providers/media-stream.ts","line":15,"issue":"MediaStreamEndedError is exported but never used/thrown anywhere in the codebase. It's defined but only referenced in tests.","suggestion":"Either use MediaStreamEndedError when appropriate (e.g., when stream ends unexpectedly during getNextFrame), or document when it would be thrown. Currently it's dead code."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/providers/video-file.ts","line":66,"issue":"MockFrameData interface is confusingly named - it's actually the internal frame data structure used by the real provider, not just for mocks.","suggestion":"Rename MockFrameData to FrameData or InternalFrameData to better reflect its