ntly with the guidance. However, this is a profile values judgment call that may need user feedback."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/profiles/pro.ts","line":151,"issue":"guideHandPosition only accepts ['side'] which is very restrictive - the test expects <= 2 options but only 1 is provided","suggestion":"This is actually correct for elite-level standards where side position is the accepted technique. No change needed, just noting the restrictiveness is intentional."}],"summary":"The implementation correctly satisfies all acceptance criteria:\n\n1. **youth-fundamentals** (youth.ts): Age-appropriate profile for ages 8-12 with wider acceptable ranges (e.g., shootingElbowAngle: 70-110° vs pro's 85-95°). Feedback uses encouraging, simple language appropriate for young players. 14 metrics focused on fundamentals.\n\n2. **high-school** (high-school.ts): Refined mechanics for ages 13-18 with tighter tolerances than youth (e.g., shootingElbowAngle: 80-100°). Adds timing metrics (ballLegSync, ballRiseStart, releaseStart) not present in youth profile. 23 metrics covering both fundamentals and rhythm.\n\n3. **pro-form** (pro.ts): Elite-level targets with tight tolerances (e.g., shootingElbowAngle: 85-95°). Comprehensive 25+ metrics covering all aspects. Technical feedback messages. Categorical targets highly restricted (e.g., only 'cup' for handCupVsHinge, only 'side' for guideHandPosition).\n\n4. **All profiles include feedback messages**: Each target has contextual tooLow/tooHigh/incorrect messages appropriate to skill level.\n\n5. **All profiles pass validation**: Tests confirm all 3 profiles pass formProfileSchema validation and safeValidateProfile. 121 tests pass.\n\n**Edge cases handled:**\n- Profile values adjustable based on user feedback (all values are configurable)\n- Youth profile excludes advanced timing metrics that aren't meaningful for development\n- Progressive tightening of ranges from youth → high school → pro\n\nCode quality is excellent with comprehensive