ofiles/comparison.ts","line":188,"issue":"Unused parameter _confidence in compareNumericMetric","suggestion":"The parameter _confidence is passed but never used (isLowConfidence is passed separately). Consider removing the unused parameter or using it directly instead of passing isLowConfidence as a separate parameter."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/profiles/index.ts","line":69,"issue":"Duplicate imports - profiles are imported twice (once for re-export at lines 61-63, once for use in the record at lines 69-71)","suggestion":"Consolidate imports at the top of the file and use a single import block for both re-export and use in builtInProfiles/allBuiltInProfiles."}],"summary":"The Profile Comparison Engine implementation is correct and comprehensive. All acceptance criteria are met:\n\n1. **compareToProfile()** compares all metrics against selected profile - metrics are iterated from profile.targets and matched against shot.metrics.\n\n2. **Pass/fail/warning status** - Correctly determined based on:\n   - Numeric values: in range = pass, outside = fail, near boundary (warning zone) = warning\n   - Categorical values: in acceptable list = pass, not in list = fail\n   - Low confidence (<0.5 default) upgrades pass to warning and downgrades fail to warning\n\n3. **Deviation calculation** - Computed as `value - ideal` for numeric metrics, undefined for categorical.\n\n4. **Corrective feedback** - Uses profile's feedback.tooLow/tooHigh/incorrect or falls back to DEFAULT_FEEDBACK_MESSAGES.\n\n5. **Priority sorting** - Issues are sorted by priority (high > medium > low) using PRIORITY_ORDER mapping.\n\n**Edge cases handled:**\n- Metric not in profile: skipped (lines 114-117)\n- Low confidence: marked as warning regardless of value (lines 226-231, 286-290)\n- Categorical comparison: uses exact string matching (line 275)\n- Type mismatch: returns fail with 'Metric type mismatch' feedback (lines 171-178)\n\nAll 44 unit tests pass. The code follows project patterns with proper TypeScript types, JSDoc documentation, and readonly properties."}}}
