stry to the index.ts exports, marked as @internal for testing purposes only."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/profiles/index.ts","line":72,"issue":"Duplicate imports - youthFundamentalsProfile, highSchoolProfile, proFormProfile are imported twice (once for re-export at lines 64-66, once for use at lines 72-74)","suggestion":"Move the imports before the exports and use a single import block for both re-export and use in builtInProfiles/allBuiltInProfiles."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/profiles/registry.ts","line":78,"issue":"The method is named 'register' but documentation and tests sometimes refer to it as 'registerProfile'","suggestion":"The current naming 'register' is actually consistent with best practices (registry.register() is cleaner than registry.registerProfile()). This is just a naming observation - the implementation is correct."}],"summary":"The Profile Management & Custom Profiles implementation is correct and meets all acceptance criteria:\n\n1. **getProfiles() → list()**: Returns a sorted array of all registered profile names (line 133-135).\n\n2. **registerProfile() → register()**: Validates profiles via Zod schema before registration, adds them to the internal Map (lines 78-92).\n\n3. **Custom profiles override built-in profiles**: When a profile with an existing name is registered, it replaces the previous one (line 91) with a console.warn (lines 84-88).\n\n4. **Invalid profiles throw validation errors**: The validateProfile() call at line 81 throws ZodError for invalid profiles.\n\n5. **Unit tests**: 44 comprehensive tests covering constructor, registration, override behavior, get/list/has methods, singleton pattern, late registration, and edge cases.\n\n**Edge cases handled correctly:**\n- Registering profile with existing name: overrides with console.warn (tested lines 248-297)\n- Empty registry: pre-populated with built-in profiles (tested lines 50-86)\n- Accessing non-existent profile: throws descriptive error listing available profiles 